{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/326341-werewolf-the-forsaken-need-ideas-on-how-a-devout-muslim-would-react-to-urathra","id":326341,"title":"[Werewolf: the Forsaken] Need ideas on how a devout Muslim would react to Urathra","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-30T15:51:41-08:00","id":326341,"title":"[Werewolf: the Forsaken] Need ideas on how a devout Muslim would react to Urathra","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Before you ask; I'm playing the Muslim in question. He's not an antagonist or NPC, he's his own character who is at least friendly enough with the People to work with them on occasion.<br /> <br /> Anyway, when 2E comes out, I'm planning on playing one of the player pack's human members and support, a Muslim lab tech who had a fateful encounter with the Beshilu and realized the sheer danger the existence of the Hosts posed to the world. Ideally, he would be an updated skinthief variant (I have it that the encounter in question was a botched attempt at Joining, causing his soul to absorb the rat's shard instead of the other way around, giving him Host-like abilities and some minor rodent traits), but a wolfblood could work too.<br /> <br /> Thing is, I have it that he's very faithful and devoted, to the point where he often wonders if he's committing grievous sins via use of sorcery, which is regarded very skeptically in the canon of Islam. So, naturally, he interprets the cosmos through the lens of Islam (&quot;Spirits? Call them what they are, jinn made from smokeless fire-what you call Essence, but I know enough of physics to tell you it's smokeless fire, just with variant fuel sources that effects the metaphysical color it burns in&quot;). He's not pushy about it, but he's not flexible about his core convictions at all (although he's the first to admit there's a lot he doesn't know that he can't pick up from holy books easily, and some of the sharia is certainly wrong; the men who wrote them were not Mohammed).<br /> <br /> So, RP question: How do you think he'd fit werewolves into his personal view of the world?</div> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T22:40:24-08:00","id":326664,"title":"","content":"The last time I played a Muslim character, things were pretty simple for her - she had a long hard look at herself and her new nature; then she had a long hard look at the way the world worked, and then she decided she was quite obviously a demon from hell. <br /> <br /> She made it her mission to hunt other, worse demons - the Forsaken way of life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T05:30:36-08:00","id":326861,"title":"","content":"I think he would probably regard werewolves as people God has called upon, given the power of the djinn (which unfortunately also comes with the passions of the djinn) and tasked with defending the human world against other more malign djinn (as well as defending the djinn's own world against unthinking interference from humans - djinn are after all children of God as well).<br /> <br /> Ie more or less what the Uratha actually are, just attributing the first causes to God.<br /> <br /> He might be more prone to see righteousness in spirits of more benign concepts like love or faith, as opposed to werewolves who see &quot;under control&quot; or &quot;lower priority threat.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T18:50:29-08:00","id":327554,"title":"","content":"Scanning through Wikipedia, I'm finding it difficult to find a fitting, positive role for them.<br /> <br /> They can't be angels, since angels have no free will. So, unless there's a fourth type of sapient creation, they must be human or jinn. I'm inclined to go with jinn as a more plausible explanation in line with the rest of his worldview, but the differences between Uratha and spirits are blatant enough that this wouldn't quite hold up to much examination. An unknown type of jinn, called forth and commanded by an unknown angel to patrol the border between the fire and clay, and in so being called forth, being twisted into clay? It doesn't fit well with First Change, but it might not have to.<br /> <br /> Dunno.<br /> <br /> A negative role is easy, though, as Christian A already shows. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T05:51:16-08:00","id":328110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/326341-werewolf-the-forsaken-need-ideas-on-how-a-devout-muslim-would-react-to-urathra?p=326861#post326861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think he would probably regard werewolves as people God has called upon, given the power of the djinn (which unfortunately also comes with the passions of the djinn) and tasked with defending the human world against other more malign djinn (as well as defending the djinn's own world against unthinking interference from humans - djinn are after all children of God as well).<br /> <br /> Ie more or less what the Uratha actually are, just attributing the first causes to God.<br /> <br /> He might be more prone to see righteousness in spirits of more benign concepts like love or faith, as opposed to werewolves who see &quot;under control&quot; or &quot;lower priority threat.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this one, personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T05:53:28-08:00","id":328113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/326341-werewolf-the-forsaken-need-ideas-on-how-a-devout-muslim-would-react-to-urathra?p=328110#post328110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like this one, personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>So do I.<br /> <br /> Thanks everyone, you've been helpful. I may not use most of these, but he's really become a lot clearer than he was before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T08:02:46-08:00","id":329235,"title":"","content":"Regarding angels: perhaps they might have the illusion of free will. After all, philosophers and some scientists argue that our decisions are made before we become conscious of them by an unknowable subconscious calculator that is interpreting our senses and reacting before the consciousness creates a sense of having chosen. It creates the potential for an interesting exploration of the theme of acting on the instinct of the Werewolf vs the disputed ability of man to make choices. One would have to be very careful to think of how the character could remain ethical rather than indulging every base whim and saying the Wolf / God made me do it but it could be a fun twist to consider one's self a tool of God and the sense of self somehow being part of the will if God (perhaps the character believes a fragment of God's will is his sense of free will) since being some form of Djinn is the path of least resistance when it comes to mental gymnastics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1881-the-cowardly-scion","name":"The Cowardly Scion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1881_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T11:56:50-08:00","id":334400,"title":"","content":"Though this raises another awkward question - are werewolves haram if they're in human form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T10:44:53-08:00","id":335322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/326341-werewolf-the-forsaken-need-ideas-on-how-a-devout-muslim-would-react-to-urathra?p=334400#post334400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though this raises another awkward question - are werewolves haram if they're in human form?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would it be sinful?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}